---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import CourtReplay from '../../components/CourtReplay';
import { href, email, courtVisionDemoUrl, courtVisionReplayUrl } from '../../lib/paths';
---
<SiteLayout title="CourtVision — Basketball coaching platform | Bryan Kwan" description="Try CourtVision’s public demo: source film, real 3D replay, shot maps, and player profiles from Toledo–Bowling Green. No account required." active="work">
  <section class="page-hero cv-page-hero"><div class="wrap">
    <a class="breadcrumb" href={href('work/')}>← All work</a>
    <div class="product-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow gold">01 / COMPUTER VISION & PRODUCT ENGINEERING</p>
        <h1>CourtVision<span class="gold">.</span></h1>
        <p class="product-tagline">The film. The floor.<br>The coaching conversation.</p>
        <p class="lede">A basketball coaching platform connecting source film, reconstructed 3D movement, shot maps, and player context. Now open to explore through a public match demo.</p>
        <div class="cv-product-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href={courtVisionDemoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try live demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="quiet-link" href="#walkthrough">Explore the 3D replay <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><span>No account required.</span></div>
        <div class="tag-list"><span class="tag">Python / Computer vision</span><span class="tag">React / TypeScript</span><span class="tag">Three.js / Blender</span><span class="tag">Cloudflare</span></div>
      </div>
      <aside class="product-brief">
        <div><span>BUILT FOR</span><p>Coaches moving between game film, player context, and the next teaching moment.</p></div>
        <div><span>MY CONTRIBUTION</span><p>The vision pipeline, coaching interface, source-driven 3D renderer, and delivery of a public demo alongside the private coaching workspace.</p></div>
        <div><span>TRY THE PRODUCT</span><p>Toledo–Bowling Green. March 12, 2026. Inspect the film, explore player profiles, and rotate reconstructed plays.</p></div>
        <div class="cv-demo-facts" aria-label="Public demo coverage"><div><strong>118</strong><span>Field-goal events</span></div><div><strong>17</strong><span>Match player profiles</span></div><div><strong>69</strong><span>Partial replay windows</span></div></div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="wrap cv-walkthrough" id="walkthrough" aria-label="CourtVision product preview">
    <div class="walkthrough-heading"><p class="eyebrow gold">THE ACTUAL REPLAY ENGINE</p><p>Real court. Real player models. A published sequence.</p></div>
    <CourtReplay client:visible />
  </section>
  <div class="wrap case-layout">
    <nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Case study chapters"><p>INSIDE COURTVISION</p><a href="#question">01 / The coaching problem</a><a href="#approach">02 / The workspace</a><a href="#evidence">03 / The system</a><a href="#limitations">04 / Current boundaries</a><a href="#artifacts">05 / Try it yourself</a></nav>
    <article class="case-body">
      <section id="question"><h2>A useful answer starts<br>with the same moment.</h2><p>A coach should be able to find a possession, inspect the source film, understand the movement, and save a useful observation without losing context between tools.</p><p>CourtVision connects those steps. The interface stays anchored to the session and moment being reviewed, while the processing pipeline keeps source evidence and human corrections connected to the output.</p></section>
      <section id="approach"><h2>A workspace built around<br>the coaching workflow.</h2>
        <div class="product-feature-grid">
          <div><span class="eyebrow gold">01 / FILM ROOM</span><h3>Find it. Watch it. Inspect it.</h3><p>A searchable event queue, outcome filters, source-film playback, shot maps, and synchronized replay keep the evidence within reach.</p></div>
          <div><span class="eyebrow gold">02 / SPATIAL REPLAY</span><h3>Go beyond a flat diagram.</h3><p>Articulated Blender player models follow reconstructed source-time poses. Rotate the court, change camera views, and scrub a play while keeping gaps and estimated depth visible.</p></div>
          <div><span class="eyebrow gold">03 / PLAYER CONTEXT</span><h3>Connect the play to the player.</h3><p>The public demo includes 17 match profiles, official match statistics, and player-specific shot maps with links back into the film room.</p></div>
          <div><span class="eyebrow gold">04 / COACH BOARD</span><h3>Keep the teaching moment.</h3><p>Draw temporarily on the court in the demo and export public match statistics. Approved coaches can also save private notes and teaching moments in their workspace.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence-note"><strong>A product you can try.</strong><p>The public demo runs the same film room and replay renderer used by the coaching workspace. Its Guide walks visitors through the actual controls, and no account is needed.</p></div>
      </section>
      <section id="evidence"><h2>From computer vision<br>to a working product.</h2>
        <div class="system-diagram" aria-label="Local processing and review feed the hosted coaching workspace and a scoped public demo">
          <div><span class="eyebrow gold">LOCAL / PYTHON</span><h3>Process & review</h3><p>Person and ball detection<br>Tracking, poses, and calibration<br>Corrections and reconstruction</p></div><span class="system-connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <div><span class="eyebrow gold">HOSTED / REACT + THREE.JS</span><h3>Inspect & coach</h3><p>Film, replay, and player context<br>Private notes and teaching moments<br>A separate public match demo</p></div>
        </div>
        <p>The processing workflow supports resumable uploads, owner approval, local inference, checkpoint recovery, and review items. The hosted coaching viewer receives versioned packages after preparation and review.</p>
        <p>Cloudflare Workers mediate access, D1 stores accounts and coaching documents, and R2 stores session media. The public demo exposes a specifically published match through read-only endpoints; private sessions and coaching documents remain in the authenticated workspace.</p>
        <div class="technical-details"><details><summary>How this portfolio preview works</summary><p>The interactive preview reuses CourtVision’s actual Three.js renderer and original Blender court and player assets. It runs a snapshot of play 004 from the public March 12 demo, with its original source-time coordinates and evidence handling.</p><p>The renderer loads only when requested. An isolated preview keeps its camera and playback independent of the portfolio’s arena. The live demo provides the complete experience, including synchronized source film.</p><ul><li>Preserve source-time poses, ball samples, and unsupported intervals.</li><li>Keep the 3D replay separate from official statistics and reviewed shot outcomes.</li><li>Start paused, support camera buttons and dragging, and pause playback when the preview leaves view.</li><li>Keep a still preview and direct demo links available if 3D cannot load.</li></ul></details></div>
      </section>
      <section id="limitations"><h2>Built to inspect.<br>Still being refined.</h2><p>The public demo covers one published match: 118 field-goal events and 69 partial replay windows. Coverage and the quality of ball, pose, event, and identity reconstruction vary by play. Missing intervals remain missing.</p><p>Rendered movement is not, by itself, proof of a correct ball path, named identity, shot result, or defensive assignment. Official match statistics and reviewed event records remain separate evidence sources.</p><p>The preview above uses a published reconstruction, not fictional player motion. It is one short example of the renderer; open the live film room to compare reconstruction against source footage and explore the rest of the match.</p></section>
      <section id="artifacts"><h2>Take it into the film room.</h2><p>Open the public workspace and try the controls yourself. Start with the overview, or jump directly to the play shown here.</p><div class="resource-links"><a class="button button-dark" href={courtVisionDemoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try live demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button" href={courtVisionReplayUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open film room <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="quiet-link" href={`mailto:${email}?subject=CourtVision%20project%20walkthrough`}>Discuss the build <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><p class="resource-caption">The demo is read-only and needs no account. Court drawings are temporary; private coaching notes, other sessions, and account tools require approved access.</p></section>
    </article>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap next-project"><a data-portfolio-return href={href('#arena-projects')} class="text-link">← Return to Home Court</a><a href={href('work/basketball/')} class="text-link">Next: the basketball decision platform <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
</SiteLayout>
